The combination of `filepath.Abs`, `filepath.Join`, `filepath.Clean`, `filepath.EvalSymlinks`, and the `strings.HasPrefix` check is a standard and generally effective way to prevent directory traversal. The `resolvedPath != absDirPath` part is also crucial. The logic seems sound for preventing access to files outside the specified `dirPath`, even through symlinks.

